# Build tooling (typescript, vite) lives in devDependencies, and both Vercel and
# Railway set NODE_ENV=production in the build environment. npm turns that into
# omit=dev, which strips the very compilers the build scripts invoke -- the
# failure looks like `sh: line 1: tsc: command not found` after an install that
# reported success. `include` overrides `omit` regardless of ordering, so the
# build container always gets what it needs to build.
include[]=dev
